<!--
Super-Kamiokande 2023 Atmospheric Neutrino Analysis Configuration
  + NATIVE BINNED-TENSOR ENGINE opt-in (pynu.binned), demonstrating the
    default-OFF <BinnedEngine> toggle (see the block in <NeutrinoExperiment>).

Identical to SK2023_Atm.xml except: (1) it adds the <BinnedEngine> block, and
(2) it scans a 2D (Dm231, Sin2Theta23) grid (the binned engine needs both osc
axes). With the toggle active, FitModel routes to FitModelBinned and the fit
runs on pre-built oscillation tensors via the engine's dCP-profiled minimizer.

NOTE (phase 1): constructing PyNuFit still runs the event truth propagation in
__init__ (needs the SK MC h5 + nuSQuIDS), so this config runs on FASRC/WARD,
not on a bare laptop. Set ${SK_BINNED_DIR} to a response+osc_tensors build.

Uses SuperK_2023 experiment class (SuperK_Atm_Pheno.py) with
SKCombinedDetector tunes. MC file: SuperK_fullMC_6_4_x50_inv_flux_tune1.h5
(3.8M events, 29 samples, SK I-V combined).

MCexposure=50 matches the x50 in filename.
Detector systematics disabled initially (decay_e_tagging MUST stay disabled
since SuperK_2023.MCVariables does not set DecayE).
-->
